<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/064D">Example <span data-tag="064D">9.2.5.4</span>.</a> The Kan complex $\Delta ^0$ corepresents the identity functor $\operatorname{id}: \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ (see Proposition <a data-tag="038P" href="/tag/038P">5.6.6.17</a>), and is therefore compact when viewed as an object of the $\infty $-category of spaces $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ (Example <a data-tag="06DN" href="/tag/06DN">9.2.2.9</a>). See Corollary <a data-tag="067U" href="/tag/067U">9.2.6.5</a> for a more general statement. </p>
